{
 "note": {
  "daily_wage": "Base amount; multiplied by the raise tier and rounded down; pay only on successful days",
  "raise_tiers": "by the number of periods this job was successful",
  "daily_effect": "fatigue is added every work day; the other effects only on a good day (user: a bad day gives no pay and changes nothing but fatigue)",
  "job_period_effect": "settled once for each successful period",
  "period_random": "prob [numerator, denominator], once per period",
  "prereq": "a cond, format in data/new/README.md",
  "success_line_mods": "when the cond holds, add value to that stat's success line (a negative value lowers it)",
  "crime_tier": "step 12c: 1 or 2. A crime job must match crime_tiers exactly (wage, crime, discipline, stamina, fatigue, search); only the skills, the success-line stats and the name may differ",
  "raid_prob": "search per successful-or-not period: prob x (1 + crime/100); then raid_skill displayed + r0(20) >= raid_line, failing means arrest",
  "wage_tiers": "Daily wage by raise tier (five tiers, dollars, 2G = $1 rounded up). The tier is picked by how many periods of this job succeeded (raise_tiers.periods_below: 8/23/45/68 = original 10/30/60/90 x 3/4). Jobs without wage_tiers use daily_wage x bonus_pct",
  "zero_one_prob": "A daily_effect range of exactly [0,1] or [-1,0] gives the non-zero value with this probability (six-year run: x4/3 of a 0-or-1 gain)",
  "bad_day": "Original roll (user, lover playtest): each success line is its own roll, displayed stat - r0(fatigue) >= value, all must hold; fatigue of the day is added before the roll. Lines are the original lines mapped to our stats; prereq still decides whether the job can be picked. The bad_day field is no longer used",
  "disabled": "true: the job is switched off (not offered, its events, milestones and NPC schedule never trigger)",
  "one_of": "daily_effect entry with one_of: the gain goes to one of these stats, picked at random each day",
  "site": "map place the job belongs to (placeholder until the user gives the locations); same site = the same place upgraded",
  "crime_job": "User (2026-11): true = a crime job (moneylending, bootlegging, the upstairs rooms). A month with one worked is searched once at month end (stats.json arrest.raid); crime_tier and raid_* belong to the old switched-off jobs"
